@title Parental leave at Tessellate
@subtitle Answers to common questions about our new policy, effective 2026-11-01
@author The People Team

Welcoming a child into your family is a big moment, and we want the time around it to be as calm as possible. This page answers the questions we hear most often. If yours is not here, we are always happy to talk.

## How much leave do I get?

- **Primary caregivers:** 16 weeks of leave at full pay.
- **Secondary caregivers:** 8 weeks of leave at full pay.

This is the same whether your child joins your family by birth, adoption or foster placement.

## Who is eligible?

You are eligible if you have worked at Tessellate for at least 6 months on the day your leave starts.

## When can I start and finish?

You can start your leave up to 2 weeks before the expected date of birth or placement. Your leave needs to be finished within 12 months of the birth or placement.

## Can I split my leave?

Yes. You can take your leave in up to 2 blocks. If you take a second block, please agree it with your manager at least 4 weeks before it starts.

## What happens to my pay, benefits and equity?

- **Pay:** you receive your full pay for the whole of your leave.
- **Health insurance:** continues, with Tessellate paying the normal employer contribution.
- **Equity:** keeps vesting while you are on leave.

## How do I come back?

You do not have to go straight back to a full week. For your first 4 weeks back you can work a transition schedule of 80 percent time at 100 percent pay, so you can settle into your new routine.

## How do I apply?

1. Tell your manager and the People Team at least 30 days before your leave starts. If your baby arrives early, just tell us as soon as you can.
2. Fill in the leave form in the HR portal.

Questions? Email [leave@tessellate.example](mailto:leave@tessellate.example) or ask in the `#people-help` channel. We are here to help.
